  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/8/3/20;--m:1/2/3/10"><div class="rte"><h2>Crisis Call</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/8/17/20;--m:3/2/34/10"><div class="rte"><p><strong>Acknowledge and show care</strong></p><p>“I’m so sorry you’re going through this right now. Your safety is very important.”</p><ol><li><p><strong>Give immediate crisis resources</strong></p><p>“I need to let you know that we are not able to provide crisis support over the phone. If you are in danger of harming yourself or others, please call <strong>988</strong> to connect with the Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline.”</p></li><li><p><strong>Provide local and text options</strong></p><p>“You can also go directly to the <strong>Wasatch Behavioral Health Receiving Center</strong> at <strong>1175 E 300 N, Provo</strong>, or to the <strong>LDS Hospital Psychiatric Access Center:</strong> <strong>324 9th Ave, Salt Lake City, UT 84103</strong> if that location is closer for you.</p></li><li><p><strong>Close with support</strong></p><p>“You are not alone in this, and reaching out was a really important step. Please call 988</p></li></ol></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
